| find horn_coral_block | (5.5, 0.5, 5.5) | 5.0 | 60° | Center of 2×2 coral block cluster; 5.0 range forces player to leave spawn (~7.8 blocks away) |
| find horn_coral | (9.0, 0.5, 5.5) | 3.0 | 60° | Center of horn coral fan group; tight 3.0 range + facing prevents overlap with coral block milestone |
| find packed_ice | (-7.0, 0.5, -6.0) | 5.0 | 60° | Center of packed ice cluster; opposite direction from coral, ~9.2 blocks from spawn |

**Anti-overlap analysis**: The horn_coral_block and horn_coral targets are 3.5 blocks apart. Even in the worst-case overlap zone (~7 blocks from spawn along the X axis), the 60° facing tolerance prevents simultaneous triggering because the two targets are in nearly opposite directions from that position (one at ~225° and the other at ~45° relative to the player).
